From 0ba4156bffb4c7e8d789f4dcf97399386596a153 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:54:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(background-agent): complete idle children when todo
 continuation is disabled

A background child that goes idle with open todos is not completed: the
session.idle handler and the poller both wait for todo-continuation to
resume it. With todo-continuation-enforcer in disabled_hooks nothing ever
resumes it, so a child whose last turn is its answer (an escalation, a
blocker report) stays "running" and its parent is not notified until the
60 min hard deadline. Observed on 2026-10-19: bg_3174f2b9 (Sisyphus-Junior)
ended on "ESCALATE: deep-high" with 4 open todos at 16:44:43Z, then logged
"Task has incomplete todos via polling, waiting" 180 times until the parent
cancelled it at 16:53:44Z.

createPluginModule now passes isHookEnabled("todo-continuation-enforcer")
through createManagers to BackgroundManager as todoContinuationEnabled
(default true). When it is false, checkSessionTodos no longer defers
completion, so an idle child with output completes and wakes its parent.
With the hook enabled nothing changes.
